#81000
"Path Through the Park"
"A pair of stately silver birches flank a rose-colored marble staircase carved
into the otherwise unbroken wall to the south, twin sentinels ever watchful
over this entrance to the inner city.  Slender posts topped with intricately
carved statuary march upwards along the stairway, each holding a tiny globe of
magical light.  Crushed gravel paths lead through the small park, stretching
to the north, west and east, each bordered by clumps of wildflowers and edged
with stone cairns.  The laughter of children at play rings through the area,
mingled with bird song and the distant sounds of the bustling city a ways to
the north.
"
"[Minqa] Climb stair acode to the south.
"
