#81002
"Path Through the Park"
"Tall, vibrantly healthy sunflowers stretch heavenwards along the western
fence, their huge blossoms oddly magenta colored instead of the more mundane
golden hue.  A row of lilies of the valley and cobalt blue hydrangeas grows
just in front of the sunflower stalks, providing a riot of brilliant color.  A
waterfall of silvery willow branches very nearly hides the entrance to a small
gazebo tucked cozily away in the southwestern corner of the area.  The perfume
of flowers and the trilling songs of the birds flitting through the treetops
overhead fill the air, lending an almost tangible sense of contentment and
tranquility to this place.
"
"[Minqa] enter gazebo acode
[Ahni] Acode done.
"
