#81003
"Path Through the Park"
"An ancient oak tree spreads its branches skywards, its gnarled trunk knobbly
and rough.  Clumps of shy violets lift their faces from beneath its roots,
revelling in the shade provided by the massive tree.  Through the latticework
of roses and ivies growing along the fence to the north, the busy streets of
Fair Havens are visible.  This place seems somehow secluded from the hustle
and bustle of the city, a sanctuary from the town's restlessness and noise. 
Oddly enough, the few creatures flying around the flowers aren't bees, but
seem to be tiny faeries, enjoying the quiet beauty of this place.
"
"[Minqa] Tree to climb
[Ahni] Acode done
"
