#81006
"Along a Crushed Marble Pathway"
"This quieter side trail leading in from ROAD to the north terminates abruptly
before an intricately carved gate of gleaming mithril.  Through the widely
spaced bars, a lush garden of roses comes into view, splashes of crimson, gold
and yellow blooming against the verdant foilage.  The small park seems nestled
into the lee of a terraced cliff, catching the early morning sun, yet cool and
well shaded in the afternoon.  The sweet perfume of flowers hangs in the air,
a pleasant change from the various odors of the rest of the city.
"
""
