#81010
"West Gate of Fair Winds"
"An impressively large gate of shimmering silver looms just to the east. 
Though obviously kept in good working order, the brightly polished silver is
carved with dainty patterns, adding a touch of elegance to the otherwise
utilarian gate.  Set above the portal, just barely visible from the ground, a
black iron portcullis lies in wait, its ebony fangs razor-sharp and ready.  A
crushed granite trail winds westward down a small hill, its path carefully
outlined by a border of mid-sized stones interspersed with clumps of
brilliantly colored flowers.
"
"[Minqa] Path southwestish to beach and sanctuary stone
"
