#81017
"Second Bank of Fair Havens"
"Panels of polished oak line the walls of this chamber.  The rugs carpeting the
wooden floor were once of high quality as well, though the passage of many
feet has worn down the nap of the carpet, and long exposure to sunlight
through the open window to the north has faded the once bright colors.  A
simple, yet elegant iron grill separates the west portion from the rest of the
room, and on the far western wall, a deep vault is set.  Before the grill is a
polished wooden counter, upon which sits a small brass bell.
