#81020
"The Bitter Moon"
"Polished bronze panels the walls of this expansive chamber, reflecting the
flickering light of dozens of candles dangling from the metal and glass
chandelier overhead.  A large fireplace stands against the western wall,
tongues of flame dancing merrily upon red-hot coals.  Most of the golden wood
floor is clear in this area of the tavern, ringed with a few tables forming an
impromtu dance floor.  Here and there, dark patches stain the polished floor,
likely the remnants of spilt ale.  Alongside the fire, a small stool of dark
mahogany sits in the shadows.  A gilded staircase spirals up towards a balcony
above, providing spectators with an excellent place to look out over the dance
floor.
"
