sanctuary, gently enfolded by the sweet fragrance of blossoms.  Only a little
illumination trickles in through the woven draperies of waxy green leaves and
golden blooms, leaving this place well shaded and cool even in the height of
summer.  The wood shaping the small gazebo has been painted a soft white
shade, worn smooth by the caresses of many hands.  High backed benches line
the walls of the gazebo, looking almost as if they had grown there.
